# Biome Enforced Rules

These rules are enforced by Biome and will error if violated.

## Formatting

- Single quotes: `'string'` not `"string"`
- Semicolons: always required
- Trailing commas: none allowed
- Line endings: LF (Unix-style)
- Indentation: 2 spaces

## Lint Rules

### No forEach
Use `for...of` instead of `.forEach()`

### Use Template Literals
Use `` `Hello ${name}` `` instead of `'Hello ' + name`

### No Floating Promises
All promises must be handled with `await` or `.catch()`

### No Unused Imports/Variables
Remove unused code - these are errors, not warnings

### Use Await
Always use `await` for async operations

### Use Date.now()
Use `Date.now()` instead of `new Date().getTime()`

### No Unused Template Literal
Don't use template literals without interpolation: `'hello'` not `` `hello` ``

### Use Block Statements
Always use braces, even for single-line blocks:

```typescript
// Good
if (condition) {
  return value;
}

// Bad
if (condition) return value;
```

### Explicit Length Check
Always use explicit comparisons:

```typescript
// Good
if (array.length === 0)
if (array.length > 0)

// Bad
if (!array.length)
if (array.length)
```

### No Yoda Expressions
Compare in natural order: `value === constant` not `constant === value`
